Z||000011||FieroJoe||09-08-2001||09:51 PM||||Unfortunatly, I work every sunday.  So does my friend, he's a new Fiero owner (I got him hooked   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ), and I'm sure he'd like to meet all of you in person.  I highly doubt if both of us would be able to get work off on the same day, since at least one of us needs to be there.  I will try, and if not maybe we can get together another saturday in october maybe just before my car (and most others) gets put away for winter projects.<P>EDIT:  Re-read ChopTop's post, and I think that it is a good idea.  Maybe we could all meet at Francis park, and ChopTop could lead the way over to Fitzgerald Park (you sound like you know where it is).  I don't know if the MFC is going to get all antsy if we show up with some of us not being members, but I don't think they should at all.  I think we should go on saturday, that way we'll have two more Fieros (me and travis, with 86 SE w/17" rims)<p>[This message has been edited by FieroJoe (edited 09-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||Tigger||09-08-2001||11:58 PM||||I don't think the MFC would have too much of a problem with non members showing.  Actually, it would probably help to get more Fiero-ites interested in joining.<P>Here's the full scoop on the MFC picnic:<P>September 22<BR>Fitzgerald Park<BR>Grand Ledge, MI<P>Park opens: 8:00am<BR>Picnic: 11:00am<BR>Riverboat Cruise: 2:00-3:00pm<P>Bring a dish to pass & table service<BR>Meat provided by club<P>RSVP to Barb Hack:  barbFiero@webtv.net  (it is important to reserve space for the Riverboat)<P>I can't guarantee non-members would be welcome, but I doubt they would turn you away.  Best thing would be to email and ask Barb.<P>I'm looking at doing the MFC picnic the 22nd.  Joe, that sounds good, I wouldn't mind meeting up at Frances Park and leave about 8:30 in the morning to caravan over.<P>Right now it looks like the forum meet is still on for Sunday the 23rd at Frances Park from 2:00 to 5:00pm.<P>As far as bringing anything, bring lawn chairs, pop, chips and whatever.  Choptop was talking about bringing a grill, I have a small one I can bring too.  If everyone brings their own hotdog - hamburger patties & buns, we'll grill em.  I'll bring some ketchup and other fixings.<P>For those who need directions to Frances Park you can find them <A HREF="http://travel.michigan.org/search/dynamic.asp?p=G21747" TARGET=_blank>here</A>.<P>Brent<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 09-09-2001).]||||reg||1
