Z||000025||ChopTop||09-12-2001||02:10 PM||||Tigger correct me if I'm wrong.<BR>Originally the Frances Park gathering was scheduled for Saturday, September 22.  However, the Michigan Fiero Club is sponsering a picnic event in Grand Ledge Fitzgeral Park on the same day (starts at 11am). Since Grand Ledge is approximately 10 to 15 miles away from Lansing it was decided it would make sense to attend their event on Saturday.  Some people are meeting at Frances Park on Saturday the 23rd (8:30), to caravan to the Fitzgerald Park picnic.<P>Unless otherwise posted in this tread, the Frances Park gathering will now be on Sunday the 23rd, 2pm-5pm.  This is a clothing optional park...yes I'm kidding!!  Bring pop, snacks, umbrellas, and wear clothes!||||reg||1
Z||000026||Tigger||09-12-2001||03:05 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ChopTop:<BR><B>Tigger correct me if I'm wrong.<BR>Originally the Frances Park gathering was scheduled for Saturday, September 22.  However, the Michigan Fiero Club is sponsering a picnic event in Grand Ledge Fitzgeral Park on the same day (starts at 11am). Since Grand Ledge is approximately 10 to 15 miles away from Lansing it was decided it would make sense to attend their event on Saturday.  Some people are meeting at Frances Park on Saturday the 23rd (8:30), to caravan to the Fitzgerald Park picnic.</B><P>Yes, but it's Saturday the 22nd<P><B>Unless otherwise posted in this tread, the Frances Park gathering will now be on Sunday the 23rd, 2pm-5pm.  This is a clothing optional park...yes I'm kidding!!  Bring pop, snacks, umbrellas, and wear clothes!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>ChopTop you don't have to bring the hamburgers and hotdogs unless you want to.  Figured you and I would bring the grills and everybody bring their own hotdogs and buns.<P>Hope to see everybody there!||||reg||1
